<title>MEXICO: Mexico says long-distance firms to invest $5.8 bln.</title>
<headline>Mexico says long-distance firms to invest $5.8 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's nine new long-distance telephone companies will invest $5.8 billion and create 17,000 jobs over the next five years, the Communications Ministry (SCT) said in a statement on Monday.</p>
<p>Mexico's long-distance telephone market will be opened to competition on January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>The SCT added that &quot;by September (1997) all lines in the country will have competitive options for these (long-distance) services.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9552</p>
